1
00:00:00,220 --> 00:00:02,480
Meta and Google, as global ad giants,

2
00:00:02,480 --> 00:00:04,740
saw a crack in their dominant hold.

3
00:00:04,840 --> 00:00:07,654
this crack allowed one firm to rise swiftly,

4
00:00:07,654 --> 00:00:10,403
with its stock soaring 25-fold in two years,

5
00:00:10,403 --> 00:00:12,825
joining the S&P 500 and the $100B club —

6
00:00:12,825 --> 00:00:14,199
that firm is AppLovin

7
00:00:14,320 --> 00:00:16,201
yet controversies and short-seller

8
00:00:16,201 --> 00:00:18,360
reports on this firm have never ceased

9
00:00:18,580 --> 00:00:20,661
this epic surge was followed by a Muddy Waters

10
00:00:20,661 --> 00:00:22,019
short-sell attack on the firm

11
00:00:22,020 --> 00:00:23,931
I think this is at least the third

12
00:00:23,931 --> 00:00:25,899
we've seen in the past month or so.

13
00:00:25,980 --> 00:00:28,019
these short-sellers are questioning

14
00:00:28,019 --> 00:00:30,000
its AI platform's trustworthiness

15
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:31,097
In early November 2025,

16
00:00:31,097 --> 00:00:33,188
I was invited to AppLovin's annual event

17
00:00:33,188 --> 00:00:34,600
at San Francisco City Hall.

18
00:00:34,770 --> 00:00:37,309
here, executives and staff, with families in tow,

19
00:00:37,309 --> 00:00:39,541
donned formal gowns and sipped champagne

20
00:00:39,541 --> 00:00:42,499
to celebrate the firm hitting a $20 billion market cap.

21
00:00:42,780 --> 00:00:45,486
Heading upstairs, the game odds laid out by the firm

22
00:00:45,486 --> 00:00:47,853
hint that the love-hate dance of Wall Street

23
00:00:47,853 --> 00:00:49,360
for AppLovin isn't over yet.

24
00:00:49,600 --> 00:00:52,547
the key figure in this game is this man—Giovanni Ge,

25
00:00:52,547 --> 00:00:55,467
the Chinese executive who nearly missed his speech

26
00:00:55,467 --> 00:00:57,980
due to a basketball clash with a colleague

27
00:01:03,380 --> 00:01:04,437
Giovanni Ge doesn't look like

28
00:01:04,437 --> 00:01:06,467
a typical Silicon Valley engineer—he graduated from the

29
00:01:06,467 --> 00:01:06,911
USTC School

30
00:01:06,911 --> 00:01:07,466
of the Gifted

31
00:01:07,466 --> 00:01:09,399
Young, earned his PhD in Italy, and then came to the US.

32
00:01:09,440 --> 00:01:10,532
after leaving Meta,

33
00:01:10,532 --> 00:01:14,236
he joined AppLovin just as it was undergoing a pivotal shift

34
00:01:14,236 --> 00:01:16,240
and led the team with key impact.

35
00:01:16,320 --> 00:01:17,520
Teach me one Italian phrase

36
00:01:17,680 --> 00:01:17,680
Buongiorno

37
00:01:18,440 --> 00:01:20,600
So tough, heh heh.

38
00:01:20,760 --> 00:01:21,640
From 2023 to 2025,

39
00:01:21,640 --> 00:01:25,160
Giovanni Ge's promotions mirrored AppLovin's stock surge

40
00:01:25,320 --> 00:01:26,895
in three years, from engineer,

41
00:01:26,895 --> 00:01:29,338
he rose swiftly to become a top tech leader

42
00:01:29,338 --> 00:01:32,520
and now serves as Chief Product and Engineering Officer.

43
00:01:32,850 --> 00:01:35,237
though there are many reports and analyses

44
00:01:35,237 --> 00:01:36,659
on AppLovin from outside,

45
00:01:36,659 --> 00:01:39,730
in-depth interviews with top executives remain scarce

46
00:01:39,900 --> 00:01:42,460
many facts and conclusions clash with one another

47
00:01:42,460 --> 00:01:44,039
when the short report first came out,

48
00:01:44,039 --> 00:01:45,180
we took it very seriously,

49
00:01:45,180 --> 00:01:47,179
cross-checking each point against our systems —

50
00:01:47,179 --> 00:01:48,780
and later found they were all wrong

51
00:01:49,010 --> 00:01:52,727
so what fascinates me about this company is that I wonder,

52
00:01:52,727 --> 00:01:56,250
how does it thrive behind giants like Meta and Google

53
00:01:56,460 --> 00:01:58,380
what did this firm do right,

54
00:01:58,380 --> 00:02:00,300
and what timing let it carve

55
00:02:00,300 --> 00:02:02,700
a niche in the giants' market space?

56
00:02:02,840 --> 00:02:05,245
We lack the resources Google and Meta have,

57
00:02:05,245 --> 00:02:08,280
so we can't use their approaches to solve our issues.

58
00:02:08,360 --> 00:02:10,448
from the moment I joined AppLovin,

59
00:02:10,448 --> 00:02:13,360
I dreamed that one day we'd move beyond games

60
00:02:13,520 --> 00:02:16,695
how does AppLovin view the praise and doubts from outside?

61
00:02:16,695 --> 00:02:18,501
How did Giovanni Ge lead his team

62
00:02:18,501 --> 00:02:21,129
in tackling the modern recommendation algorithm?

63
00:02:21,130 --> 00:02:23,260
the toughest challenge here was finding staff.

64
00:02:23,260 --> 00:02:24,880
the market didn't trust us much.

65
00:02:24,880 --> 00:02:27,860
That year, hiring was extremely tough—just very, very hard.

66
00:02:27,980 --> 00:02:29,462
driven by this curiosity,

67
00:02:29,462 --> 00:02:30,903
we at 'Silicon Valley 101'

68
00:02:30,903 --> 00:02:33,973
did an exclusive video interview with Giovanni Ge,

69
00:02:33,973 --> 00:02:35,580
his first ever in Chinese.

70
00:02:35,740 --> 00:02:37,580
the past three years felt like a decade;

71
00:02:37,580 --> 00:02:39,420
each day was a battle. In Silicon Valley,

72
00:02:39,420 --> 00:02:42,180
I believe the underdog spirit is the most cherished one here.

73
00:02:42,220 --> 00:02:46,080
Our interview with Giovanni Ge was filmed on Dec 21, 2025

74
00:02:46,320 --> 00:02:48,597
the full interview lasted over two hours,

75
00:02:48,597 --> 00:02:49,430
yet to be frank,

76
00:02:49,430 --> 00:02:52,320
our conversation at times felt a bit back-and-forth

77
00:02:52,510 --> 00:02:55,296
The reason is, I desperately wanted to know —

78
00:02:55,296 --> 00:02:58,150
what did AppLovin do right to rise so fast?

79
00:02:58,340 --> 00:02:59,752
but I found this was not

80
00:02:59,752 --> 00:03:02,460
how Giovanni Ge and AppLovin framed the issue

81
00:03:02,540 --> 00:03:03,702
I noticed when we chatted,

82
00:03:03,702 --> 00:03:04,547
you wanted to know

83
00:03:04,547 --> 00:03:07,132
if our success stemmed from just one specific decision —

84
00:03:07,132 --> 00:03:08,260
but that's not the case.

85
00:03:08,340 --> 00:03:10,163
The decision itself was simple;

86
00:03:10,163 --> 00:03:12,103
what drove the company to success

87
00:03:12,103 --> 00:03:13,809
was the 365 days that followed.

88
00:03:13,810 --> 00:03:15,193
How do we live each day?

89
00:03:15,193 --> 00:03:16,980
Outsiders always seek an answer

90
00:03:16,980 --> 00:03:19,229
to make our success seem simple indeed.

91
00:03:19,390 --> 00:03:21,500
I find such doubts and undervaluing

92
00:03:21,500 --> 00:03:23,430
have become quite routine to me.

93
00:03:23,510 --> 00:03:24,061
In Q1 2026,

94
00:03:24,061 --> 00:03:26,082
AppLovin continued facing attacks

95
00:03:26,082 --> 00:03:27,860
from short-sellers once more

96
00:03:27,940 --> 00:03:29,463
AI's threats to ad sectors,

97
00:03:29,463 --> 00:03:32,100
plus rivals vying for market share dominance

98
00:03:32,280 --> 00:03:33,935
After U.S. stocks closed on Feb 11,

99
00:03:33,935 --> 00:03:36,160
AppLovin released its Q4 2025 earnings report

100
00:03:36,360 --> 00:03:37,836
revenue, profits, and outlook

101
00:03:37,836 --> 00:03:38,835
all beat analysts'

102
00:03:38,835 --> 00:03:41,280
forecasts—this was a stellar earnings report.

103
00:03:41,420 --> 00:03:43,841
yet the stock price plummeted sharply;

104
00:03:43,841 --> 00:03:46,771
this divergence hints at capital markets' fears

105
00:03:46,771 --> 00:03:47,918
that AI may upend

106
00:03:47,918 --> 00:03:48,619
SaaS firms.

107
00:03:48,780 --> 00:03:50,983
At this moment, we launch this interview,

108
00:03:50,983 --> 00:03:53,379
aiming to gain insights from Giovanni Ge's

109
00:03:53,379 --> 00:03:56,860
in-depth reflections on the past three years—roughly 1,000 days.

110
00:03:57,060 --> 00:04:00,860
how he led AppLovin to split giants' grip and cross the chasm

111
00:04:00,920 --> 00:04:05,399
How did this firm rise amid Google and Meta's duopoly?

112
00:04:05,399 --> 00:04:07,804
And how did it break through

113
00:04:07,804 --> 00:04:10,640
using the 'underdog' mindset? First?

114
00:04:10,640 --> 00:04:13,309
Before we dive into Giovanni Ge's interview,

115
00:04:13,309 --> 00:04:16,600
let's spend a moment on AppLovin's business and rise.

116
00:04:20,579 --> 00:04:22,582
In 2018, Silicon Valley's digital ad

117
00:04:22,582 --> 00:04:24,586
landscape was rigid—Google ruled

118
00:04:24,586 --> 00:04:25,437
search intent,

119
00:04:25,437 --> 00:04:27,260
Meta controlled social graphs.

120
00:04:27,460 --> 00:04:28,427
at that time,

121
00:04:28,427 --> 00:04:32,540
AppLovin was just a small mobile ad network player.

122
00:04:32,720 --> 00:04:34,746
in short, it's a middleman platform

123
00:04:34,746 --> 00:04:36,501
linking mobile app developers —

124
00:04:36,501 --> 00:04:38,680
the ad space hosts — with advertisers.

125
00:04:38,840 --> 00:04:43,134
for such a 'middleman,' the fatal flaw is that it has no clue

126
00:04:43,134 --> 00:04:45,800
what users are doing inside the app.

127
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:49,706
Think—how can you compete with giants like Google and Meta

128
00:04:49,706 --> 00:04:51,880
if you lack first-party user data?

129
00:04:52,200 --> 00:04:53,586
To break this stalemate,

130
00:04:53,586 --> 00:04:56,480
AppLovin began aggressively buying game studios.

131
00:04:56,680 --> 00:04:59,240
from 2018 up till just before its IPO

132
00:04:59,480 --> 00:05:03,032
AppLovin rapidly expanded via M&A, strategic investments,

133
00:05:03,032 --> 00:05:04,453
and studio incubation,

134
00:05:04,453 --> 00:05:07,360
with game deals totaling billions of dollars

135
00:05:07,400 --> 00:05:09,520
and via its ad and distribution platforms,

136
00:05:09,520 --> 00:05:12,520
it reached hundreds of millions of mobile users worldwide.

137
00:05:12,660 --> 00:05:15,496
At the time, AppLovin bought these studios

138
00:05:15,496 --> 00:05:16,950
not for game profits,

139
00:05:16,950 --> 00:05:19,580
but to capture key conversion signals

140
00:05:19,810 --> 00:05:20,975
these 'in-house' games

141
00:05:20,975 --> 00:05:23,890
served as the early labs for the algorithm engine

142
00:05:24,150 --> 00:05:28,036
At the same time, AppLovin made a series of key acquisitions.

143
00:05:28,036 --> 00:05:31,469
The first was MAX, the in-app bidding tech firm, in 2018.

144
00:05:35,260 --> 00:05:39,700
Before 2018, AppLovin was essentially an ad-serving platform.

145
00:05:39,920 --> 00:05:43,470
but for developers, it didn't help them fetch top prices

146
00:05:43,470 --> 00:05:45,600
for their ad inventory very well.

147
00:05:45,810 --> 00:05:46,402
At the time,

148
00:05:46,402 --> 00:05:49,690
the most common method in the industry was 'Waterfall Layout'.

149
00:05:49,920 --> 00:05:51,884
In short, developers would first try

150
00:05:51,884 --> 00:05:53,737
offering ad slots to platform A;

151
00:05:53,737 --> 00:05:56,319
if A declined, then try B, and if B failed, try C.

152
00:05:56,360 --> 00:06:01,008
one after another, in a preset order based on past eCPM ,

153
00:06:01,008 --> 00:06:04,710
or effective cost per thousand impressions

154
00:06:04,800 --> 00:06:07,760
and fill rate , along with other historical metrics

155
00:06:07,880 --> 00:06:11,496
the problem is that this process is queue-based, slow,

156
00:06:11,496 --> 00:06:14,070
and often sells slots for low prices

157
00:06:14,420 --> 00:06:15,590
Once MAX came along,

158
00:06:15,590 --> 00:06:19,100
the rules changed completely—it added in-app RTB bidding.

159
00:06:19,260 --> 00:06:21,671
drop the ad slot to all advertisers at once,

160
00:06:21,671 --> 00:06:24,980
let them bid simultaneously, and sell to the highest bidder

161
00:06:25,240 --> 00:06:27,488
developers just get top bids straight away,

162
00:06:27,488 --> 00:06:28,880
and income jumps right up

163
00:06:29,080 --> 00:06:32,409
advertisers aren't worse off—say they spent ¥1.50,

164
00:06:32,409 --> 00:06:35,600
but if they earn ¥2 back, it's still a good deal.

165
00:06:35,720 --> 00:06:37,656
The result? Developers earned more,

166
00:06:37,656 --> 00:06:41,000
and advertisers got better users—both sides were pleased.

167
00:06:41,160 --> 00:06:42,402
Thanks to MAX, AppLovin

168
00:06:42,402 --> 00:06:45,315
evolved from a 'just-for-buyers' role into a platform

169
00:06:45,315 --> 00:06:47,600
serving both advertisers and developers.

170
00:06:47,720 --> 00:06:50,060
the second major acquisition was in 2021,

171
00:06:50,060 --> 00:06:53,120
when $1 billion was spent to buy Adjust, a mobile app

172
00:06:53,120 --> 00:06:55,040
data tracking and marketing firm

173
00:06:58,860 --> 00:07:02,646
in the ad industry, advertisers care about just one thing:

174
00:07:02,646 --> 00:07:06,499
how much return can I get from every single dollar I spend.

175
00:07:06,660 --> 00:07:10,180
but in mobile ads, this question is quite hard to answer.

176
00:07:10,360 --> 00:07:13,248
because an ad goes from being shown to clicked,

177
00:07:13,248 --> 00:07:14,567
then downloaded, used,

178
00:07:14,567 --> 00:07:17,080
and even paid for—many steps in between

179
00:07:17,200 --> 00:07:20,322
and these data points are often scattered across systems

180
00:07:20,322 --> 00:07:21,159
or just unseen

181
00:07:21,240 --> 00:07:24,080
for advertisers, this feels like a black box indeed.

182
00:07:24,180 --> 00:07:27,085
by contrast, platforms that track data more clearly—like

183
00:07:27,085 --> 00:07:29,780
Meta—can more easily secure funds from advertisers

184
00:07:29,920 --> 00:07:32,600
AppLovin's growth thus faced certain limitations as well.

185
00:07:32,720 --> 00:07:35,440
and Adjust precisely solves this very issue

186
00:07:35,660 --> 00:07:39,500
Adjust is a mobile ad tracking and attribution tool at core

187
00:07:39,720 --> 00:07:42,825
it offers full-funnel tracking and precise attribution,

188
00:07:42,825 --> 00:07:46,032
helping advertisers see exactly where each dollar spent

189
00:07:46,032 --> 00:07:47,082
delivers results —

190
00:07:47,082 --> 00:07:48,519
like where the money went

191
00:07:48,760 --> 00:07:50,840
how many users came, and how much profit was made

192
00:07:50,960 --> 00:07:52,207
and more importantly,

193
00:07:52,207 --> 00:07:55,764
this data can then be fed back into AppLovin's AI system

194
00:07:55,764 --> 00:07:57,200
to refine ad targeting.

195
00:07:57,490 --> 00:08:00,477
Adjust helped AppLovin evolve from a platform

196
00:08:00,477 --> 00:08:02,602
that merely served ads into one

197
00:08:02,602 --> 00:08:04,887
that, from the client's perspective,

198
00:08:04,887 --> 00:08:07,980
could be accountable for campaign performance.

199
00:08:08,220 --> 00:08:11,460
that is why AppLovin places great emphasis on LTV

200
00:08:11,460 --> 00:08:11,460
v.

201
00:08:11,620 --> 00:08:12,905
that is lifetime value.

202
00:08:12,905 --> 00:08:16,257
We'll discuss this in detail during our exclusive interview.

203
00:08:16,257 --> 00:08:17,597
The MAX and Adjust moves

204
00:08:17,597 --> 00:08:20,559
have propelled AppLovin into a phase of rapid growth.

205
00:08:20,680 --> 00:08:24,960
Yet just as AppLovin completed its IPO in April 2021,

206
00:08:25,160 --> 00:08:30,035
Apple's IDFA, or the ATT policy, ended cross-app user tracking,

207
00:08:30,035 --> 00:08:34,179
plunging the mobile ad market into chaos overnight.

208
00:08:34,380 --> 00:08:36,960
In 2022, AppLovin's stock plummeted,

209
00:08:36,960 --> 00:08:39,380
dropping 80% from its prior peak.

210
00:08:39,500 --> 00:08:41,359
yet amidst this widespread turmoil,

211
00:08:41,359 --> 00:08:43,164
AppLovin did not, like its rivals,

212
00:08:43,164 --> 00:08:46,120
cut costs by laying off staff to tighten its defenses

213
00:08:46,320 --> 00:08:50,280
but made a key acquisition from Twitter at that time instead

214
00:08:54,240 --> 00:08:58,095
this $1.05 billion all-cash deal acquired MoPub,

215
00:08:58,095 --> 00:09:02,740
the mobile ad platform that was once part of Twitter.

216
00:09:02,740 --> 00:09:05,404
You can think of it as a 'big ad space marketplace.'

217
00:09:05,404 --> 00:09:07,375
It aggregates ad slots from many apps,

218
00:09:07,375 --> 00:09:10,359
sells them to advertisers, and takes a cut in the middle.

219
00:09:10,520 --> 00:09:12,297
this acquisition brought about three

220
00:09:12,297 --> 00:09:13,680
very clear and major shifts.

221
00:09:13,920 --> 00:09:16,600
First, it can reach far more people right away

222
00:09:16,960 --> 00:09:20,640
At the time, MoPub served tens of thousands of apps,

223
00:09:20,640 --> 00:09:23,553
including news, tools, and lifestyle apps,

224
00:09:23,553 --> 00:09:25,720
reaching about 700 million DAU

225
00:09:25,900 --> 00:09:28,650
once AppLovin integrated these ad slots,

226
00:09:28,650 --> 00:09:32,078
the ad inventory surged by an order of magnitude,

227
00:09:32,078 --> 00:09:34,080
and reach doubled overnight

228
00:09:34,320 --> 00:09:37,200
Second, ads can reach the 'right' audience segments

229
00:09:37,480 --> 00:09:38,506
MoPub's ad slots

230
00:09:38,506 --> 00:09:41,649
weren't just from games—they came from news apps,

231
00:09:41,649 --> 00:09:44,280
fitness apps, and lifestyle tools as well

232
00:09:44,400 --> 00:09:45,874
this means female users,

233
00:09:45,874 --> 00:09:49,080
middle-aged users, and non-gamers are now included.

234
00:09:49,320 --> 00:09:52,086
ads are no longer 'one ad for every person,'

235
00:09:52,086 --> 00:09:54,920
but tailored to match different audiences

236
00:09:55,100 --> 00:09:58,148
AppLovin, too, has evolved from a gaming ad platform

237
00:09:58,148 --> 00:10:01,014
into a full-fledged, cross-industry ad network.

238
00:10:01,014 --> 00:10:03,819
Third, it's now more stable and more profitable.

239
00:10:04,220 --> 00:10:07,715
before, AppLovin's ad slots mainly came from its own games,

240
00:10:07,715 --> 00:10:09,187
as we mentioned earlier,

241
00:10:09,187 --> 00:10:11,580
and the user base skewed toward gamers

242
00:10:11,780 --> 00:10:15,182
with MoPub, AppLovin no longer needs to churn out games

243
00:10:15,182 --> 00:10:16,820
just to generate ad slots.

244
00:10:17,060 --> 00:10:18,000
A clever analogy:

245
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:20,387
it shifted from growing your own veggies

246
00:10:20,387 --> 00:10:21,880
to running a supermarket,

247
00:10:21,880 --> 00:10:24,820
with stock from all corners—stable and manageable

248
00:10:25,010 --> 00:10:28,079
To sum it up, Max solves the issue of poor pricing,

249
00:10:28,079 --> 00:10:30,425
Adjust AS tackles unclear performance,

250
00:10:30,425 --> 00:10:33,090
and More Pop addresses insufficient scale.

251
00:10:33,280 --> 00:10:36,416
Meanwhile, this MoPub acquisition brought AppLovin

252
00:10:36,416 --> 00:10:38,720
a crucial and vital new data source.

253
00:10:39,040 --> 00:10:41,506
these constant, real-time bid signals

254
00:10:41,506 --> 00:10:45,480
laid the groundwork for enhancing the algorithms later on.

255
00:10:45,620 --> 00:10:46,435
At this point,

256
00:10:46,435 --> 00:10:50,260
AppLovin urgently needed a top-tier algorithm expert to join

257
00:10:50,500 --> 00:10:52,795
so after those three key acquisitions,

258
00:10:52,795 --> 00:10:55,340
AppLovin sought yet another leap forward.

259
00:10:55,500 --> 00:10:56,859
So this is a major backdrop

260
00:10:56,859 --> 00:10:58,622
in AppLovin's development history.

261
00:10:58,622 --> 00:10:59,226
At this time,

262
